      "text": "To determine the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\), we first need to find the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\).\n\n### Step 1: Find the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\)\n\nWe perform the division of 1 by 7:\n\\[\n1 \\div 7 = 0.\\overline{142857}\n\\]\nThis tells us that the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\) is a repeating decimal with the repeating block \"142857\".\n\n### Step 2: Identify the length of the repeating block\n\nThe repeating block \"142857\" has 6 digits.\n\n### Step 3: Determine the position of the 100th digit\n\nTo find the 100th digit, we need to determine the position of 100 within the repeating block. We do this by finding the remainder when 100 is divided by the length of the repeating block:\n\n\\[\n100 \\div 6 = 16 \\text{ remainder } 4\n\\]\n\nThe remainder is 4, which means that the 100th digit corresponds to the 4th digit in the repeating block \"142857\".\n\n### Step 4: Identify the 4th digit in the repeating block\n\nThe repeating block is \"142857\". The 4th digit in this block is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
